From 85e3dfda07be3784cf9edcd5410656c3b70fb33a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:40:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sf: fast e-ink mode while the screen moves or the keyboard is
 up

For the XRZ e-ink composer (Bigme HiBreak Pro), which takes its refresh
mode from vendor.xrz.global_refresh_mode on every commit. Its NORMAL mode
(DU) shows a frame about every 120 ms, FAST (A2) about every 36 ms; both
run on the kernel's self-cleaning path.

With debug.sf.eink_motion=1, SurfaceFlinger sets the property to FAST
when three composites follow each other within 150 ms, or while the input
method's layer is visible. 700 ms after the last frame, once the kernel
has finished cleaning up after the FAST frames, it puts the
previous mode back and repaints once, so the still screen is drawn in the
mode the user chose. If someone else changes the property meanwhile, that
value becomes the mode to return to.

vendor.xrz.hibreak_motion_fast and vendor.xrz.hibreak_ime_fast switch the
two triggers; debug.sf.eink_motion.{mode,frames,gap_ms,end_ms} tune it.
---
 services/surfaceflinger/Android.bp            |   1 +
 .../DisplayHardware/EinkMotion.cpp            | 161 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../DisplayHardware/EinkMotion.h              |  81 +++++++++
 services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp    |  22 +++
 4 files changed, 265 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 services/surfaceflinger/DisplayHardware/EinkMotion.cpp
 create mode 100644 services/surfaceflinger/DisplayHardware/EinkMotion.h

